{"uid":"2782ed30d94f2e75","name":"test_v09_iteration_185_regression_reflect_past_the_deadline_still_reports","fullName":"tests.test_reflect_tail_budget#test_v09_iteration_185_regression_reflect_past_the_deadline_still_reports","historyId":"e4c81b620f369a8d58c2e5526dc0c041","time":{"start":1791891691791,"stop":1791891691839,"duration":48},"description":"Reproduces `selfdev-v09-fsm-loop`'s exact shape: by the time reflect\n    gets its one attempt, the job's deadline is already gone (there, review\n    183 and planning 184 burned the last of it; here, the deadline is set\n    in the past before the job even starts, so `_step_planning`'s own\n    `budget_left()` guard sends the job straight to the terminal tail with\n    no agent call at all -- the fastest way to reach \"reflect is the only\n    iteration that runs, with the deadline already behind it\"). Before this\n    task's fix, reflect's own attempt got the 60s floor same as every other\n    phase and this scenario is exactly what starved it; now it must produce\n    a real report.\n\n    Task 011 (v0.24 requirement C.1, #169) repointed that exact guard at\n    `_finish_timed_out()` -- a hold, not a terminal outcome, so no reflect\n    iteration follows it at all now (by design, task 010, requirement\n    B.3). A pre-recorded operator abort (`self._abort_reason` set before\n    `run_job()`) is layered on top so this scenario still lands on an\n    ordinary terminal tail (`\"aborted\"`) that DOES still run reflect --\n    the one thing this test actually pins.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Reproduces <code>selfdev-v09-fsm-loop</code>'s exact shape: by the time reflect<br />\ngets its one attempt, the job's deadline is already gone (there, review<br />\n183 and planning 184 burned the last of it; here, the deadline is set<br />\nin the past before the job even starts, so <code>_step_planning</code>'s own<br />\n<code>budget_left()</code> guard sends the job straight to the terminal tail with<br />\nno agent call at all -- the fastest way to reach &quot;reflect is the only<br />\niteration that runs, with the deadline already behind it&quot;). Before this<br />\ntask's fix, reflect's own attempt got the 60s floor same as every other<br />\nphase and this scenario is exactly what starved it; now it must produce<br />\na real report.</p>\n<pre><code>Task 011 (v0.24 requirement C.1, #169) repointed that exact guard at\n`_finish_timed_out()` -- a hold, not a terminal outcome, so no reflect\niteration follows it at all now (by design, task 010, requirement\nB.3). A pre-recorded operator abort (`self._abort_reason` set before\n`run_job()`) is layered on top so this scenario still lands on an\nordinary terminal tail (`&quot;aborted&quot;`) that DOES still run reflect --\nthe one thing this test actually pins.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791891119391,"stop":1791891119391,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791891119392,"stop":1791891119392,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791891691730,"stop":1791891691749,"duration":19},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791891691730,"stop":1791891691730,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":fa